# Architecture

KIRABAKI is a **modular monolith**. No microservices. No custom LLM. No vector DB until retrieval is proven slow.

- `app/` — routes and layouts only
- `domains/` — identity, finance, accounts, transactions, assets, liabilities, goals, knowledge, rules, analysis, recommendations, commitments, outcomes, snapshots, ai, audit
- `tax/`, `receipts/`, `business/` — stub until those phases
- `lib/money` — deterministic calculations only (pure, tested)
- `lib/db`, `lib/auth` — persistence and Better Auth
- `ai/prompts/` — versioned prompts when an LLM exists

**Four-layer Brain (never violate):**

1. Deterministic engine — balances, cashflow, net worth, projections = code
2. Versioned rules — inspectable if/then, not hidden in prompts
3. Knowledge — structured principles with provenance (not PDF dumps)
4. LLM — explain and synthesise only; never invent numbers or override Layer 1

UI never owns formulas. Presentation never queries the DB. Domain logic is independently testable.

Postgres is the system of record. PWA is the client. See `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` and `docs/PLATFORM-AND-SCALE.md`.
